		{
			dependencies: ["14B46980C5503330"]
			description: [
				"What good is colliding stuff if you can't observe what is happening?"
				""
				"Along the rings you will build &6detector complexes&r, each tuned to produce data if the beam is at the correct &aenergy level, luminosity,&r and &atype of collision&r. The detectors you will build will be based off the real ones at the &dLHC&r, and possibly feature future less realistic ones for the sake of the modpack."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"From the official page:"
				""
				""
				"&6ATLAS &7(A Toroidal LHC ApparatuS)"
				"&bCMS &7(Compact Muon Solenoid)"
				"&aLHCb &7(Large Hadron Collider beauty experiment)"
				"&dALICE &7(A Large Ion Collider Experiment)"
				"&9TOTEM &7(Total Cross Section, Elastic Scattering and Diffraction Dissociation)"
				"&eLHCf &7(LHC forward) &6(ATLAS Attachment)"
				"&cMoEDAL &7(the Monopole and Exotics Detector At the LHC)"
				"&3FASER &7(Forward Search Experiment)"
				"&5SND &7(Scattering and Neutrino Detector)"
				"&2CODEX-b &a(LHCb Attachment)"
			]
			icon: "compactmachines:wall"
			id: "4BC4922AEBF81C8F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3012A3DB8E240A44"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Detectors"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4BC4922AEBF81C8F"]
			description: [
				"To increase rate of science, you need to collide &amore stuff&r &6more harder&r &bmore faster&r. "
				""
				"Rings inherently have &cspeed limits&r since turning the beam causes it to lose a bit of speed. The only real way around this is having a &dlarger ring&r so this loss is well, less."
				""
				"As you progress existing rings will &estop being producers&r and &asimply tie into new larger rings&r, sending each other beams until whatever is the largest ring in your factory does the work."
			]
			icon: "compactmachines:wall"
			id: "6BFED9DFAB88AB58"
			tasks: [{
				id: "196CF5F0B0B6EA33"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Rings On Rings"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"0D6FCB630A560E67"
				"6BFED9DFAB88AB58"
			]
			description: [
				"With sufficient advances in capturing collision products, you now have an interesting chance here to produce a catalyst for nuclear fusion with a beam of &dmuons&r."
				""
				"&dMuons&r belong to the same family of electrons &7(Leptons)&r and such can form atoms in a similar way."
				""
				"The key difference here is that &cmuons&r are much &eheavier&r than electrons &7(105.66 MeV vs 0.511 MeV)."
				""
				"When a muonic atom forms, &7in this case muonic hydrogen&r, the &melectron&r muon cloud is so small that fusion can happen at &aroom temperature&r. The cool sci-fi \"cold fusion\"."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now the problem here is producing a muon takes &cmore energy&r than the amount of fusion events it can trigger before &cdecaying&r."
				""
				"Clearly not useable for the entire reaction but with a nice hot beam of muons it can surely be part of the &6ignition&r, and more importantly, breeding of rare isotopes needed to sustain the reaction."
			]
			icon: "compactmachines:wall"
			id: "70419BDF2E69C429"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6CDAC42F149AC31F"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Muon Catalyst"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["41C9A53B03DF4A33"]
			description: [
				"Superconducting materials are able to have &n&6zero&r electrical resistance."
				""
				"This is incredibly useful for base infrastructure, but more importantly &bmagnets&r."
				""
				"Superconducting magnets are the key to getting your particle accelerators and magnetic confinement upgraded."
				""
				"The downside is all known superconductors either need &9cryogenic temperatures&r, or &cinside of planets level pressures&r."
				""
				"This means, until you can make some truly &dexotic compounds&r, your magnets will themselves need infrastructure! Yay!"
			]
			icon: "pneumaticcraft:magnet_upgrade"
			id: "76657F5544B89CE8"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4C512494A6530421"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Superconducting Hell"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"70419BDF2E69C429"
				"6F1CE2A93AD7E92A"
			]
			description: [
				"After you build your massive toroidal magnet with a &dmuon beam blasting in&r, filled with &atritium and duterium&r, &6liquid lithium flowing along the walls&r, and a really&b hot and angry proton LINAC blasting the chamber&r you can achieve ignition! A little baby star is born."
				""
				"Now that was a lot of work, whats it all for?"
				""
				"A lot actually."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"For one your &aenergy issues are largely solved&r for a very long time. "
				""
				"Your fuel source is &bwater&r now as well, so hopefully you got a few dozen ocean hexes laying around still."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As for advancing your factory supplies, &6everything before iron on the periodic table is up for grabs&r from base hydrogen. "
				""
				"Heavier elements past hydrogen will need higher temperatures which means better confinement tech, heating systems, and beefier LINAC ignition. But that will be a self contained improvement loop with science."
				""
				"All of these processes will be &apower positive&r, the most energetic being on the hydrogen side, &eslowly decreasing&r until manganese. (one before iron)."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Iron fusion and above will be &cpower negative&r."
				""
				"Reliably the heaviest thing that can be produced at huge cost will be Zirconium."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Beyond that point you'll need proper &cneutron star conditions&r to get much else done."
				""
				"But ok we have the oreline, &n&lwhy is this useful&r?"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The utility here is the fusion reactions will let you make ex-nihilo&6 specific isotopes of elements&r, which will be needed for &abombardment experiments&r and &bconducting more research&r."
				""
				"What research?"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c&l&oBombs&r"
				""
				"Full proper momentary star, country cracking, hydrogen bombs."
				""
				"I mean, I think it's about time we at least tried to chip some of that &5Flake&r. Good place to start I recon."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:nether_star"
			id: "471FED5AA87D2F3B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "368E9101AEC30760"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "IGNITION!"
			x: -11.5d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"76657F5544B89CE8"
				"4BC4922AEBF81C8F"
			]
			description: [
				"Neutron absorbing techology is already used in &dTier 5&r but was mostly about controlling the fission reactions and not really about capturing the energy from them directly outside of boiling some water."
				""
				"Here catching the &6ultra hot neutrons&r from fusion will be how you actually get energy out of the system. "
				""
				"This also means the internal blanket of the reactor must be resistant to &eneutron flux&r while also allowing neutrons to either pass through it, or itself absorb them."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Another issue to consider is that a large chunk of the material for the blanket will become &cactivated&r overtime and will need to be replaced, introducing the need to basically rip your reactor apart every once in a while to gut and replace the blanket."
			]
			icon: "compactmachines:wall"
			id: "2BDBCB8A28CF8049"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4DCBD29A2ED6EBFF"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Neutron Absorbers"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2BDBCB8A28CF8049"]
			description: [
				"The issue of the blanket leads into a fun solution. &6Liquid Lithium&r!"
				""
				"By having the walls of the reactor internally be &aswirling liquid lithium&r you can avoid the issue of sputtering from tungsten while also serving as a &bbreeding medium&r."
				""
				"When a neutron slams into the lithium it will spit out &btritium&r, which is fusion fuel."
				""
				"Naturally keeping liquid lithium swirling around the walls while &cseveral hundred million degree plasma&r sits centimeters away wont be trivial but, thats \"just\" an engineering problem."
			]
			icon: "chemlib:lithium"
			id: "4F32E2A23F08BB0E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4B5A706D4633FF26"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Breeding Blanket"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["76657F5544B89CE8"]
			description: [
				"Superconducting Magnets will need &9liquid nitrogen or colder&r to exist in-world next to it in order to function."
				""
				"Some systems will have &cliquid helium&r as a hard requirement."
				""
				"This is a mechanic introduced all the way back in &6Tier 2&r but here will be the true large scale construction and maintenence of said mechanic. Enjoy!"
			]
			icon: "chemlib:helium"
			id: "22D826F87313D555"
			tasks: [{
				id: "236E9144C4B53823"
